hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1466","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Do not turn away from your forefathers, for whoever turns away from his father has committed disbelief."
"1467","narrates about the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that one day, while mentioning prayer, he said: ""Whoever performs them regularly, they will be light, proof, and salvation for him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever does not perform them regularly, he will have no proof, no light, and no salvation, and on the Day of Resurrection, he will be with Qarun, Haman, and Ubayy bin Khalaf."
"1468","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever misses one prayer, it is as if his family and wealth have been destroyed."
"1469","The Messenger of Allah said: ""The one who misses the 'Asr prayer, it is as if he has been cheated out of his family and wealth."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 685)"
"1470","The Sheikh states that Imam Awza'i made a mistake in his Sahifah by narrating this report from Yahya bin Abi Kathir from Abu Qilabah. He said that it is narrated from Abu Muhajir, whereas the narrator's name is Abu Muhallab, who is the uncle of Abu Qilabah, and his name is Amr bin Mu'awiyah bin Zayd al-Jarmi."
"1471","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in praying 'Asr in Al-Mukhammas. He said: 'This prayer was enjoined upon those who came before you, but they neglected it. Whoever prays it regularly will have a two-fold reward, and there is no prayer after it until the Shahid appears."" And the Shahid is ""the star."" [1] [1] This is a statement of one of the narrators, and Allah knows best. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 521)"
"1472","""Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet ﷺ when the sun had passed its zenith and said: 'Get up, O Muhammad, and pray Zuhr when the sun has passed its zenith.' Then he waited until a man's shadow was equal to his height. Then he came to him for 'Asr and said: 'Get up, O Muhammad, and pray 'Asr.' Then he waited until the sunset, then he came to him and said: 'Get up, O Muhammad, and pray Maghrib.' So he got up and prayed it when the sun had set. Then he waited until the twilight disappeared, then he came to him and said: 'Get up, O Muhammad, and pray 'Isha'.' So he got up and prayed it. Then he came to him when dawn broke and said: 'Get up, O Muhammad, and pray.' So he got up and prayed Subh.' So he got up and prayed Subh. Then he came to him the next day when a man's shadow was equal to his height, and said: 'Get up, O Muhammad, and pray.' So he prayed Zuhr. Then Jibril came to him when a man's shadow was equal to twice his length and said: 'Get up, O Muhammad, and pray.' So he prayed 'Asr. Then he came to him for Maghrib when the sun set, at exactly the same time as the day before, and said: 'Get up, O Muhammad, and pray.' So he prayed Maghrib. Then he came to him for 'Isha' when the first third of the night had passed, and said: 'Get up and pray.' So he prayed 'Isha'. Then he came to him for Subh when it had become very bright, and said: 'Get up and pray.' So he prayed Subh. Then he said: 'The times of prayer one between those two (limits).'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 526)"
"1473","The time for Zuhr is when the sun declines and a man's shadow is equal to his height (this remains) until the time for Asr begins. The time for Asr remains until the sun becomes yellow. The time for Isha remains until midnight. (Regarding one word here, the narrator is in doubt.) And the time for Fajr is until the sun rises."
"1474","Prayer at its appointed hour. I (again) said: Then what? He (the Holy Prophet) replied: Kindness to the parents. I (again) said: Then what? He replied: Earnest endeavour (Jihad) in the cause of Allah. And I would have not ceased asking more questions but out of regard (for his feelings). (Using translation from Muslim 85a)"
"1475","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To perform the prayer at its earliest time."
"1476","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To perform the prayers at their prescribed times."" I asked, ""Then which one?"" He said: ""Then to show kindness to parents."" I asked, ""Then which one?"" He said: ""Then striving (jihad) in the way of Allah."" (Sayyiduna Abdullah narrates) If I had asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) further, he would have given me more answers."
"1477","I had asked for more, he would have given more answers. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Abu Amr Shaibani is among the Mukhadramin; when a person has spent sixty years in the time of disbelief and sixty years in the time of Islam, he is called a Mukhadram."
"1478","Prayer at its appointed hour. I (again) said: Then what? He (the Holy Prophet) replied: Kindness to the parents. I (again) said: Then what? He replied: Earnest endeavour (Jihad) in the cause of Allah. And I would have not ceased asking more questions but out of regard (for his feelings). (Using translation from Muslim 85a)"
"1479","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""To perform the prayer at its earliest time."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In narrating these words, 'to perform the prayer at its earliest time,' Uthman bin Umar is unique among the narrators."
"1480","""We complained to the Messenger of Allah about the heat of the sunbaked ground, but he did not respond to our complaint."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 676)"
"1481","Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal, the Messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us in Yemen, I heard his takbir (utterance of AllahuAkbar) in the dawn prayer. He was a man with loud voice. I began to love him. I did depart from him until I buried him dead in Syria (i.e. until his death). Then I searched for a person who had deep understanding in religion amongst the people after him. So I came to Ibn Mas'ud and remained in his company until his death. He (Ibn Mas'ud) said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: How will you act when you are ruled by rulers who say prayer beyond its proper time? I said: What do you command me, Messenger of Allah, if I witness such a time? He replied: Offer the prayer at its proper time and also say your prayer along with them as a supererogatory prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 432)"
"1482","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You should perform the prayer at its prescribed time, and if you find those people and they have not yet performed the prayer, then perform the prayer with them as well. Do not say, 'I have already performed the prayer, so I will not pray now.'"
"1483","If anyone obtains a rak'ah in the prayer (along with the imam), he has obtained the whole prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1121)"
"1484","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever catches one rak'ah of the morning prayer before the sun rises, his prayer has not been missed. Whoever catches one rak'ah of the Asr prayer before the sun sets, his prayer has not been missed."
"1485","If anyone obtains a rak'ah in the prayer (along with the imam), he has obtained the whole prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1121)"
"1486","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Whoever catches one Rak’ah of prayer, he has caught it.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1122)"
"1487","""Whoever catches up with a Rak'ah of the prayer, then he has caught up with it."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 554)"
"1488","A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ while we were with him. She said: Messenger of Allah, my husband, Safwan ibn al-Mu'attal, beats me when I pray, and makes me break my fast when I keep a fast, and he does not offer the dawn prayer until the sun rises. He asked Safwan, who was present, about what she had said. He replied: Messenger of Allah, as for her statement ""he beats me when I pray"", she recites two surahs (during prayer) and I have prohibited her (to do so). He (the Prophet) said: If one surah is recited (during prayer), that is sufficient for the people. (Safwan continued:) As regards her saying ""he makes me break my fast,"" she dotes on fasting; I am a young man, I cannot restrain myself. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on that day: A woman should not fast except with the permission of her husband. (Safwan said:) As for her statement that I do not pray until the sun rises, we are a people belonging to a class, and that (our profession of supplying water) is already known about us. We do not awake until the sun rises. He said: When you awake, offer your prayer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2459)"
"1489","Sayyiduna Rafi' bin Khadij narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \""You people should perform the morning prayer with the morning (light), because whenever you perform the morning prayer with the morning (light), it will be more virtuous for your reward. (The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) for its reward.\"" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Here the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has commanded to perfo"
"1490","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Offer the Fajr prayer when it becomes bright, for it is more rewarding."
"1491","The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these words are: “It is a cause for increasing your rewards.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by his statement “make it bright” meant the moonlit nights in which the appearance of true dawn is not clear. The reason for this is that a person should offer the Fajr prayer at a time when he is certain that it has become bright due to the appearance of true dawn, because when the prayer is offered in the manner we have described, it will be more rewarding than if a person offers the prayer without being certain of the appearance of true dawn."
"1492","""A man came to the Prophet and asked him about the times of the prayer. He said: 'Pray with us for two days.' When the sun passed its zenith he commanded Bilal to call the Adhan, then he commanded him to give the Iqamah for Zuhr; then he commanded him to give the Iqamah for 'Asr when the sun was high and clearly white. Then he commanded him to give the Iqamah for Maghrib when the sun had set; then he commanded him to give the Iqamah for 'Isha' when the red afterglow had disappeared; then he commanded him to give the Iqamah for Fajr when dawn came. On the following day he commanded him to give the Adhan for Zuhr when the extreme heat had passed and it had cooled down; then he prayed 'Asr when the sun was still high, but he delayed it more than he had done the day before; then he prayed Maghrib before the red afterglow disappeared; he prayed 'Isha' when one-third of the night had passed; and he prayed Fajr at the time when it was already light. Then he said: 'Where is the one who was asking about the times of Prayer?' The man said: 'Here I am, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'The times of your prayer are between the times you have seen.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 667)"
"1493","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in the morning prayer (Fajr) one day. He performed it in darkness, then the next day he performed it in brightness. Then he said: Where is the person who asked about the time of the prayer? (The time of this prayer) is between these two prayers which we performed yesterday and today."
"1494","The narrator says: He counted on his fingers and mentioned this about the five prayers. (Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates:) I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the Zuhr prayer when the sun had declined, and when the heat was intense, sometimes he would delay it. I saw him perform the Asr prayer when the sun was still high and bright, and no yellowness had entered it, and a person, after performing this prayer, could reach Dhul-Hulaifah before the sun set. He would perform the Maghrib prayer when the sun had set, and the Isha prayer when the horizon had become dark. Sometimes he would delay this prayer until, when the people gathered (he would then perform it). He would perform the Fajr prayer in darkness, then later, several times, he performed it in brightness. After that, he continued to perform this prayer in darkness until he passed away. He never performed this prayer in brightness again."
"1495","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in prayer. He performed it in darkness, then the next day he led us in prayer and performed it in light. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Where is the person who asked about the time of the morning prayer? (The time of this prayer is) between the two prayers which we performed yesterday and today."
"1496","I turned towards Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) and I asked: Which prayer is this? He replied: This is our prayer performed following the example of the Prophet (peace be upon him), Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). When Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was martyred, Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) began to perform it in the light."
"1497","The narrator says: We asked Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) how much time there was between their finishing sahur and beginning the Fajr prayer, so Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: As long as it takes a person to recite fifty verses."
"1498","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say the Fajr prayer after which the women would depart wrapped up their woolen garments, being unrecognizable because of the darkness before dawn. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 423)"
"1499","narrates: Believing women would wrap themselves in their sheets and perform the Fajr prayer behind the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), then they would return to their homes. Due to the darkness, they could not be recognized."
"1500","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would lead the morning prayer, then the believing women would come out (of the mosque) wrapped in their cloaks, and due to the darkness, they could not be recognized."
"1501","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would lead the morning prayer, and the women would wrap themselves in their sheets and return. Due to the darkness, they could not be recognized."
"1502","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) went out and led the Zuhr prayer after the sun had declined."
"1503","Sayyiduna Abu Barzah Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him). My father"
"1504","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Indeed, heat is a part of the scorching of Hell, so perform the prayer at a cooler time.\"""""""
"1505","We were praying Zuhr with the Messenger of Allah at the time of intense heat (i.e., midday when the sun has just passed its zenith) and he said to us, ""Wait for it to cool down before you pray, for intense heat is from the flaring up of the Hell-fire."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 680)"
"1506","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'When it is very hot, then wait for it to cool down before you pray, for intense heat is from the flaring up of the Hell-fire.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 677)"
"1507","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If it is very hot, wait until it cools down before you pray, for intense heat is a breeze from Hell.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 500)"
"1508","We were praying Zuhr with the Messenger of Allah at the time of intense heat (i.e., midday when the sun has just passed its zenith) and he said to us, ""Wait for it to cool down before you pray, for intense heat is from the flaring up of the Hell-fire."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 680)"
"1509","The muezzin intended to give the call to prayer for the Zuhr prayer, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: Let it cool down. Then he intended to give the call to prayer, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: Let it cool down. This happened two or perhaps three times, until we saw the shadows of the hills. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The severity of the heat is part of the heat of Hell, so when the heat is intense, perform (the Zuhr) prayer at a cooler time. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Abu al-Hasan Ubaid bin Hasan is a Muhajir from Kufa."
"1510","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When it is hot, make delay (in the noon prayer) till it cools down, for the intensity of beat is from the Exhalation of Hell; and he also mentioned that Hellfire complained to the Lord (about the congested atmosphere) and so it was permitted to take two exhalations during the whole year, one exhalation during the winter and one exhalation during the summer. (Using translation from Muslim 617b)"
"1511","narrates: We used to offer the Friday prayer behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when there were no walls whose shade we could come under."
"1512","We used to observe the Friday prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the sun passed the meridian. and we then returned and tried to find out afternoon shadow (of the walls for protecting themselves from the heat of the sun). (Using translation from Muslim 860a)"
"1513","""We used to pray Jumu'ah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ then we would go back and tend to our camels."" I said: "" At what time?"" He said: ""When the sun had passed its zenith."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1390)"
"1514","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performing this prayer in this (time) manner; I will never abandon it."
"1515","narrates: We used to perform the ‘Asr prayer behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then after that a camel would be sacrificed and divided into ten portions and then cooked. We would eat that cooked meat before the sun set. And in the blessed time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we used to perform the Maghrib prayer, and after finishing the prayer, a person could see the place where his arrow had fallen (i.e., there was still that much light at that time)."
"1516","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in the Asr prayer. When he finished the prayer, a man from the tribe of Banu Salamah came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah! We want to sacrifice our camel and we wish that you also come there. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) set out and we also went with him. When we reached there, we found that the camel had not yet been sacrificed. Then it was sacrificed, its meat was cut, then it was cooked, and before the sun set, we had eaten it."
"1517","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif narrates: We performed the Zuhr prayer behind Umar bin Abdul Aziz, then we left from there and went to the service of Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), and we found him performing the Asr prayer. I said: O uncle, which prayer is this that you have performed? He replied: This is the prayer of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), the prayer which we used to perform behind him (peace be upon him). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Amr bin Yahya Mazni narrated this report from Khalid bin Khallad, who is related to Banu Najjar. He narrates: I performed the Zuhr prayer behind Umar bin Abdul Aziz, then I went to the service of Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) and found him performing the Asr prayer. When he completed the prayer, I said: Which prayer have you performed? He said: Asr. I said: We have just come after performing the Zuhr prayer behind Umar bin Abdul Aziz. He said: I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performing this prayer in this manner, so I will never abandon it."
"1518","Anas b. Malik said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say the 'Asr prayer when the sun was high and bright and living, then one would go off to al-'Awali and get there while the sun was still high. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 404)"
"1519","The Messenger of Allah used to pray 'Asr when the sun was still hot and high, and if a person were to go to the suburbs (of Al-Madinah) he would be able to reach it while the sun was still hot and high. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 682)"
"1520","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would perform the Asr prayer while the sun was still high and bright. Then a person would go towards ""Awali,"" he would reach ""Awali"" and the sun would still be high."
"1521","It was narrated from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed 'Asr when the sun was in her room and the shadow had not appeared on her wall. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 505)"
"1522","Anas b. Malik said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say the 'Asr prayer when the sun was high and bright and living, then one would go off to al-'Awali and get there while the sun was still high. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 404)"
"1523","Salama b. al-Akwa' reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray the evening prayer when the sun had set and disappeared (behind the horizon). (Using translation from Muslim 636)"
"1524","'Mu'adh bin Jabal would pray Al-Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah, then he would return to his people to lead them (in prayer)."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 583)"
"1525","""A man came to the Prophet and asked him about the times of the prayer. He said: 'Pray with us for two days.' When the sun passed its zenith he commanded Bilal to call the Adhan, then he commanded him to give the Iqamah for Zuhr; then he commanded him to give the Iqamah for 'Asr when the sun was high and clearly white. Then he commanded him to give the Iqamah for Maghrib when the sun had set; then he commanded him to give the Iqamah for 'Isha' when the red afterglow had disappeared; then he commanded him to give the Iqamah for Fajr when dawn came. On the following day he commanded him to give the Adhan for Zuhr when the extreme heat had passed and it had cooled down; then he prayed 'Asr when the sun was still high, but he delayed it more than he had done the day before; then he prayed Maghrib before the red afterglow disappeared; he prayed 'Isha' when one-third of the night had passed; and he prayed Fajr at the time when it was already light. Then he said: 'Where is the one who was asking about the times of Prayer?' The man said: 'Here I am, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'The times of your prayer are between the times you have seen.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 667)"
"1526","""I am the most knowledgeable among the people about the prescribed time of this prayer: Messenger of Allah would pray it when the moon set on the third (of the month)."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 165)"
"1527","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to delay the later 'Isha'.""[1] [1] It is described as the later 'Isha' prayer because the Maghrib prayer is sometimes called 'Isha' prayer, but it is the first 'Isha'. Some scholars are of the opinion that it is disliked to call Maghrib 'Isha' without qualifying it as the first 'Isha'. See Fath Al-Bari. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 533)"
"1528","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) about the prayer of the Prophet (peace be upon him), so he informed us that he used to offer the Zuhr prayer after the sun had declined, and the Asr prayer when the sun was still bright, and the Maghrib prayer when the sun had set, and sometimes he would offer the Isha prayer early and sometimes delay it. When people would come early, he would offer it early, and when people did not come early, he would delay it, while he used to offer the Fajr prayer in darkness."
"1529","I would have delayed this prayer until midnight."
"1530","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “At this time, besides you, there is no follower of any religion who is remembering Allah, the Exalted.” Upon this, this verse was revealed: “They are not all alike. Among the People of the Book is a community that recites the verses of Allah in the hours of the night, prostrating themselves.” This verse continues up to: “they prostrate.”"
"1531","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Were I not afraid that it would be hard on my followers, I would order them to use the siwak (as obligatory, for cleaning the teeth). (Using translation from Bukhārī 7240)"
"1532","The Prophet (peace be upon him) came out—this scene is still before my eyes—water droplets were dripping from his head, and he had his hand placed on his head. He said: ""If I did not fear hardship for my ummah, I would have commanded them to perform this prayer at this time."
"1533","I did not fear hardship for the believers, I would have commanded them to perform this prayer (i.e., at this time)."
"1534","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to delay the later 'Isha'.""[1] [1] It is described as the later 'Isha' prayer because the Maghrib prayer is sometimes called 'Isha' prayer, but it is the first 'Isha'. Some scholars are of the opinion that it is disliked to call Maghrib 'Isha' without qualifying it as the first 'Isha'. See Fath Al-Bari. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 533)"
"1535","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ deferred one night the 'Isya' prayer. And this is called 'Atama. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not come out till Umar b. Khattab told (him) that the women and children had gone to sleep. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out towards them and said to the people of the mosque: None except you from the people of the earth waits for it (for the night prayer at this late hour), and it was before Islam had spread amongst people. And in the narration transmitted by Ibn Shihab the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is reported to have said: It is not meant that you should compel the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for prayer. And (this he said) when 'Umar b. Khattab called (the Holy Prophet) in a loud voice. (Using translation from Muslim 638a)"
"1536","""We stayed in the Masjid one night waiting for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to pray 'Isha'. He came out to us when one-third of the night or more had passed, and he said when he came out: 'You are waiting for a prayer for which the followers of no other religion are waiting. Were it not that I would impose too much difficulty on my Ummah, I would have led them in prayer at this time.' Then he commanded the Mu'adhdhin to say the Iqamah and he prayed."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 537)"
"1537","I can still see it before my eyes today. The narrator says: Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) raised his left hand and said this."
"1538","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Were it not that it would be too difficult for my Ummah, I would have delayed the 'Isha' prayer until one third or one half of the night had passed.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 691)"
"1539","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Were it not that it would be too difficult for my Ummah, I would have delayed the 'Isha' prayer until one third or one half of the night had passed.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 691)"
"1540","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Were I not afraid that it would be hard on my followers, I would order them to use the siwak (as obligatory, for cleaning the teeth). (Using translation from Bukhārī 7240)"
"1541","The desert Arabs may not dominate you in respect of the name of your prayer. Beware! It is al-ʿIsha, but they milk their camels when it is fairly dark. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4984)"
"1542","“Safwan bin Mu’attal asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: ‘O Messenger of Allah, I want to ask you about something of which you have knowledge and I know nothing.’ He said: ‘What is it?’ He said: ‘Is there any time of the night or day when it is disliked to perform prayer? He said: ‘Yes, when you have prayed the Subh, then do not pray until the sun has risen, for it rises between the two horns of Satan. Then pray, for the prayer is attended (by the angels) and is acceptable (to Allah) until the sun is right overhead like a spear. For at that time Hell is heated up and its gates are opened. (Then refrain from prayer) until the sun passes the zenith. Then when it has passed the zenith, the prayer is attended (by the angels) and is acceptable (to Allah) until you pray the ‘Asr. Then stop praying until the sun has set.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1252)"
"1543","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade performing prayer after the ‘Asr prayer until the sun sets, and after the Fajr"
"1544","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade performing prayer after the ‘Asr prayer until the sun sets, and after the Fajr prayer un"
"1545","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When the edge of the sun appears, do not perform prayer until it has fully risen, then you may perform prayer. Then when the edge of the sun sets, do not perform prayer until it has completely set, then you may perform prayer. And do not fix the time of your prayer for the time of sunrise or sunset (i.e., do not perform prayer at that time), because it rises between the two horns of Satan."
"1546","There were three times at which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid us to pray or bury our dead - when the sun begins to rise till it is fully up, when the sun is at its height midway till it passes the meridian, and when the sun draws near to setting till it sets, or as he said. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3192)"
"1547","“Do not pray after ‘Asr unless you pray when the sun is still high.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 1073)"
"1548","""No one of you should deliberately try to pray when the sun is rising, or when it is setting."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 563)"
"1549","Some reliable people testified before me, and among them was Umar ibn al-Khattab, and most reliable in my eyes was Umar: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: There is no prayer after the dawn prayer until the sun rises; and there is no prayer after the 'Asr prayer until the sun sets. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1276)"
"1550","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When you have performed the morning prayer, then refrain from performing prayer until the sun rises high, because it rises between the two horns of Satan. After that, (the angels’) attendance is present in the prayer, and it is accepted, until it is midday. When it is midday, then refrain from performing prayer until the sun declines; this is the time when Hell is kindled, and the intensity of heat is a part of the heat of Hell. When the sun declines, (the angels’) attendance is present in the prayer, and it is accepted, until you perform the Asr prayer. When you have performed the Asr prayer, then refrain from performing prayer until the sun sets, because it sets between the two horns of Satan. After that, (the angels’) attendance is present in the prayer, and it is accepted, until you perform the morning prayer."
"1551","""There are three times at which the Messenger of Allah forbade us to pray or to bury our dead: When the sun has risen fully until it is higher, when it reaches its zenith until it has passed the zenith, and when the sun starts to set"" (Sahib) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2013)"
"1552","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O descendants of Abdul Muttalib! If (the responsibility of overseeing the affair"
"1553","Sayyiduna Jubair bin Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: \""O Banu Abd Manaf! Do not prevent anyone who wishes to perform Tawaf of this House or to pray near it at any hour of the night or day.\"""""""
"1554","Sayyiduna Jubair bin Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: \""O Banu Abd Manaf! Never prevent any person who is performing Tawaf of this House at any hour of the night or day, nor anyone who is praying near it.\"""""""
"1555","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""If anyone forgets a prayer he should pray that prayer when he remembers it. There is no expiation except to pray the same."" Then he recited: ""Establish prayer for My (i.e. Allah's) remembrance."" (20.14). (Using translation from Bukhārī 597)"
"1556","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through its time, then when he remembers it, he should perform it."
"1557","The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever catches one Rak'ah of the 'Asr before the sun sets, then he has caught it, and whoever catches one Rak'ah of the Subh before the sun rises, then he has caught it."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 699)"
"1558","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): ""Soon there will come rulers who will ruin the prayer; they will make it as narrow as the brightness of a dead body. So whoever among you finds them, let him perform the prayer at its specified time, and make his prayer with them a voluntary (nafl) prayer."
"1559","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughaffal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Between the two calls to prayer (i.e., the adhan and the iqamah), prayer is performed. This (instruction) is for the one who wishes; between the two calls to prayer (i.e., the adhan and the iqamah), prayer is performed—this (instruction) is for the one who wishes.\"" The narrator named Ibn Buraidah used to perform two rak‘ahs before Maghrib as well."""""
"1560","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Between the two calls to prayer (i.e., the adhan and the iqamah), prayer is to b"
"1561","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughaffal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Between the two calls to prayer (i.e., the adhan and the iqamah), prayer will be performed (this command is for the one who wishes to perform this prayer).\"""""""
"1562","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No prayer should be offered after ʿAsr unless the sun is bright and still high.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 610)"
"1563","The Prophet (peace be upon him) kept looking at him, but did not object to him."
"1564","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the prayer. When he completed the prayer, there were two men behind the people (who had not performed the prayer in congregation with the Prophet). By the order of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), both of them were brought, and their bodies were trembling. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked them: What is the reason that you both did not perform the prayer with us? Both of them replied: O Messenger of Allah! We had already performed the prayer at our place of residence, then we came here. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When you have performed the prayer at your place of residence and then you find the (congregational) prayer (with the Imam), then perform the prayer; it will be counted as a voluntary (nafl) prayer for you."
"1565","I attended Fajr prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Masjid al-Khayf. When he finished praying, he saw two men at the back of the people who had not prayed with him. He said: “Bring them here.” So they were brought to him, trembling. He said: “What kept you from praying with us?” They said: ‘O Messenger of Allah ﷺ we had already prayed in our homes.' He said: “Do not do that. If you have already prayed in your homes, then you come to a masjid in which there is a congregation, then pray with them, and it will be a voluntary prayer for you."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 858)"
"1566","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: ""No person should attempt to perform prayer when the sun is near rising or when the sun is near setting."
"1567","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the edge of the sun becomes visible, refrain from prayer until it has fully risen (i.e., completely come out), and when the edge of the sun is about to disappear, refrain from performing prayer until it has completely set."
"1568","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade performing prayer at the time when the sun is rising."
"1569","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not try to perform prayer at the time of sunrise or at the time of sunset, because it sets between the two horns of Satan."
"1570","We bear witness that 'Aishah said: Not a day passed but the Prophet ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs after the 'Asr prayer (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1279)"
"1571","""I heard Masruq and Al-Aswad say: We bear witness that 'Aishah said: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with me after 'Asr, he would pray them (these two Rak'ahs).'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 576)"
"1572","narrates: Will someone be punished because of these two rak'ahs? Whenever the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) used to come to my house, he would perform these two rak'ahs."
"1573","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) never abandoned performing two rak'ahs after Asr in my house, until he departed from this world."
"1574","narrates: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was unable to perform the two rak‘ahs after Zuhr due to some engagements, he would perform them after ‘Asr."
"1575","I was not able to perform them until this time."
"1576","The time when he performed these rak‘ahs was when he came to me after performing the ‘Asr prayer. At that time, some women from the Ansar tribe of Banu Haram were present with me. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed these two rak‘ahs, so I sent a girl to him and instructed her: Stand beside the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and say to him that Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) is saying: O Messenger of Allah! I have heard you forbidding the performance of these two rak‘ahs, and now I am seeing you performing them. If the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) signals to you with his hand, then step back. The girl reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) signaled with his blessed hand, so I stepped back. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) explained: O daughter of Abu Umayyah! You have asked about the two rak‘ahs after ‘Asr. Some people from the tribe of ‘Abd al-Qays came to me on behalf of their people regarding Islam. They did not allow me to perform the two rak‘ahs after Dhuhr. These are the same two rak‘ahs."
"1577","""He used to pray them before 'Asr, but if he got distracted or forgot them, he would pray them after 'Asr, and if he did a prayer he would be constant in it."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 578)"
"1578","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Do as many deeds as you are able, for Allah’s bounty will not be cut off from you until you become weary. (Lady Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates) The most beloved deed to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was that which was done regularly, even if it was little. Whenever the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performed a prayer, he would perform it regularly. Abu Salamah narrates: Allah the Exalted has said: “Those who are regular in their prayers.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), “Indeed, Allah does not tire until you tire,” is among those expressions whose intended meaning cannot be comprehended by the addressee’s knowledge (i.e., what attribute is meant according to Allah’s majesty, a person cannot know)."
"1579","Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I will wake you all up. Then he sat down leaning against his mount. The Prophet (peace be upon him) woke up when the edge of the sun had already risen. He said: O Bilal! What happened to what you said? He replied: Sleep also overcame me, and it was such a sleep as I have never experienced before. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Get up and announce the prayer among the people. When the sun had risen and become bright, the Prophet (peace be upon him) stood up and led the people in prayer."
